WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:02.801
-Ladies and gentlemen, over the
weekend we were saddened to hear

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:04.367
the news that our friend
legendary journalist

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.334
Barbara Walters had passed.

00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:07.634
She was a great friend
of the show,

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:09.801
and I was lucky to get to know
her over the years.

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:13.534
I'll share with you one story
that you might find funny.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:15.567
Don't vote on it.
But, yeah, just --

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:16.968
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.968 --> 00:00:20.200
Back in the "Late Night" days, I
got the opportunity to interview

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.868
President Obama.

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:25.501
So as any smart talk show host
would do, I wanted to be

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.200
as prepared as possible
for this interview.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.601
So I called three people
for help.

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:31.968
I called Jay Leno, Howard Stern,
and Barbara Walters.

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.701
Jay Leno gave me his advice,
which was to set the president

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.501
up with some jokes, keep the
interview funny. That was good.

00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:40.133
Howard Stern said,
"Ask him about his sex life."

00:00:40.133 --> 00:00:41.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:43.934
And do they go on dates?
I mean, how do they do things

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:45.367
around with all the
Secret Service agents

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:46.534
and everyone's watching them?

00:00:46.534 --> 00:00:48.868
I go, "It's probably
a very interesting topic,

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:51.234
but I can't get away
with asking that."

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:53.801
So I got a number for
Barbara Walters and I called it

00:00:53.801 --> 00:00:56.334
around 4:00 p.m.
on a Sunday afternoon.

00:00:56.334 --> 00:00:58.601
And she picks up the phone.
It's Barbara Walters' voice.

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.300
She goes, "Hello?"
I go, "Hi, Barbara.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.767
This is Jimmy Fallon.
Thank you for taking my call."

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:05.000
She said, "Jimmy, I will have to
call you back.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.200
It is Sunday and I'm about to
take my bubble bath."

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:13.801
I go, "Awesome, okay."

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:16.300
And so I said, "Okay."

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.601
And then she called me back,

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:20.167
and she goes, "Okay, here's
an interesting question.

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:21.767
I think this could be
interesting.

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:23.200
He lives in the White House
with his wife,

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.167
his mother-in-law,
his two daughters.

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:27.367
Besides the dog, he's
the only male in the family

00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:29.267
at the White House.
What is that like?"

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:31.300
And she nailed it.
That was a great question.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.000
I used it. That was my opener.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.167
So I wanted -- I thanked her
for that, and I thanked her

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:37.634
for helping me
and for the great advice.

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:39.934
And after that she came on
the show a bunch of times.

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:42.601
And I did keep asking her
if she would want to do

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.567
a bathtub interview with me
talking...

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:47.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:49.234
...in a giant bathtub
with bubbles.

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:52.601
And it was probably until her
third appearance, she said,

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:55.100
"Jimmy, I'm coming on the show,
but please don't ask me again

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.534
about the bubble bath
interview."

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:58.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:00.367
She was a legend in journalism

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:02.234
and in television
and throughout her career.

00:02:02.234 --> 00:02:04.701
She always did it with dignity,
class, and a sense of humor.

00:02:04.701 --> 00:02:07.000
Always very interesting,
always very charming.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.634
I don't know what her secret
was,

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:10.100
but maybe it was the bubbles.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.300
We will miss our dear friend
Barbara Walters.

